        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0367" n="295" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg295"/>

                <head>No. 144.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoppin to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-09-29"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 29,
                        1882</date>. (Received October 12.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 254.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Lowell’s No. 434, of the
                    30th of August last, I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy of a letter
                    which I received to-day from Lord Granville, in relation to the arrests of Mr.
                    Henry George and Mr. Stephen J. Meany in Ireland. It will be observed that his
                    lordship after explaining the circumstances which led to the arrest of Mr.
                    George, expresses the regret of Her Majesty’s Government at the occurrence.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. J. HOPPIN.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d199-a1.xml" xpointer="d199-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
